    "html_sha256": "5ace3093035efa89919c6243f12bc64d3f8370817f1af55af87fb6d87493909f",
    "excerpt": "The caption panel shows what VoiceOver is speaking, and can be helpful when sharing your Mac with sighted users. Note: VO represents the VoiceOver modifier that you press with additional keys to enter VoiceOver commands. By default, you can press Control and Option together or just press Caps Lock. Show or hide the panel Do one of the following: Open VoiceOver Utility (press VO-Fn-F8 when VoiceOver is on), click the Visuals category, click Panels and Menus, then select the “Show caption panel” checkbox. Open VoiceOver Utility for me Press VO-Fn-Command-F10 to show or hide the panel. To show or hide the caption panel, the braille panel, and the VoiceOver cursor, press VO-Fn-Command-F11. Move or resize the panel Press VO-Shift-Fn-F10 until you hear the action you want to perform. For example, if you hear “resizing” but you want to move the caption panel, press the keys again to hear “moving.” Press the VoiceOver modifier with the arrow keys to move or resize the caption panel. When you’re done, press the Escape key or Fn-Tab. See also Tile visuals to focus on the VoiceOver cursor on Mac Use the VoiceOver braille panel on Mac Change VoiceOver Visuals settings (Panels and Menus tab) in VoiceOver Utility on Mac Download this guide in Braille Ready Format: BRF (English) Previous Use the trackpad gestures rotor Next Use the screen curtain Helpful? Yes No Character limit: 250 Please don’t include any personal information in your comment. Maximum character limit is 250. Submit Thanks for your feedback. Apple Footer  Apple Support VoiceOver User Guide Use the VoiceOver caption panel on Mac United States Copyright © 2026 Apple Inc. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy Terms of Use Sales and Refunds Site Map"
